# Anchored per repo rule: never bare, unanchored patterns.
#
# One entry per worker was how this started, and it is how an 8.9 MB
# `.wrangler/tmp` dev bundle reached a public repo on 2026-08-22: the spike
# added a new worker directory before anyone added its ignore rule, and
# `git checkout <ref> -- <path>` does not consult ignores anyway. These
# single-level wildcards are still anchored, and they cover the worker
# directory nobody has created yet.
/node_modules/
/*/node_modules/
/*/.wrangler/
/*/.dev.vars
